+## F7 — The tourguide Sentry lane is one info-level heartbeat, and the collector's signature collapses every `Error` into one bucket (NEW; Stage-1 design)
+
+With the lane live (F1), 28 days of tourguide Sentry data contain **exactly
+one issue, every day**: `7658752743`, signature
+`_selfheal__mechanical_cron_outcome_no_action`, 11–13 events per 24 h window
+(the 2-hourly self-heal cron), `first_seen` 2026-09-04T22:00:25Z. Source:
+`cloudflare/worker/src/utils/self_heal.mjs:181-183` — `captureMessage(
+"[selfheal] mechanical_cron outcome=no_action", { level: "info" })` on every
+run with nothing to do. The collector asks Sentry for `is:unresolved` with
+no `level:` filter (`herdr-control/lib/engineering-ledger.sh:73-76`), so an
+informational heartbeat is the lane's permanent top issue. No other
+tourguide issue has appeared in 28 days — consistent with either a clean
+worker or with F6's 84 swallowing catches; the lane cannot distinguish.
+
+Second design limit, visible in F3's data: `safe_sig` takes the issue title
+up to the first `:` (`engineering-ledger.sh:102-107`). Sentry titles
+exceptions `Type: message`, so every `throw new Error(...)` in thurber-ai
+lands in the ledger as `Error` — the 22-event burst on 09-11 is unattributable
+for this reason, and two unrelated bugs would share one signature.
+
+**Classification: auto-diagnose-alert-only**; both are herdr-control build
+decisions (**never-automate** to change): (a) add `level:error` (or
+`!level:info`) to the Sentry query, or have tourguide record the heartbeat
+as a breadcrumb/metric rather than a message; (b) fold Sentry's `culprit`
+or `metadata.function` (sanitized through the existing `safe_sig`) into the
+signature. Neither is in the allowlist.
